The M comparisons have passed against both earlier evaluators, and the S/L GPU checks are progressing. The launcher tests cover explicit tier selection, automatic binding of the attempt’s `args.json`, metadata tampering, and final hash revalidation.

The probe launcher now runs one S/L arm and writes a receipt with a failing status if it is contaminated or projects above 60 hours. I’m wiring the receipt into the full-run deadline and epoch-1 guard next.
